---
import { jevChecks, piBenchmark } from "~/data/optimising";

const CALLS = [3, 4, 5, 6, 7] as const;
const fewer = Math.round((1 - piBenchmark.optimised.meanCalls / piBenchmark.stock.meanCalls) * 100);
const slower = (piBenchmark.optimised.medianSeconds - piBenchmark.stock.medianSeconds).toFixed(1);

const arms = [
  { key: "stock", label: "Stock Pi", counts: piBenchmark.stock.calls },
  { key: "optimised", label: "My profile", counts: piBenchmark.optimised.calls },
] as const;

/** The race replays the measured times at a fifth of real speed. */
const REPLAY = 0.2;
const lanes = [
  { label: "One after another", seconds: jevChecks.serialSeconds },
  { label: "In parallel", seconds: jevChecks.parallelSeconds },
];
---

<div class="work">
  <article class="item" aria-labelledby="pi-title">
    <header>
      <h3 id="pi-title">A leaner coding harness</h3>
      <p class="status">Pi, with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash. Not public yet.</p>
    </header>

    <figure class="waffles" data-reveal>
      {
        arms.map((arm) => (
          <div class:list={["arm", arm.key]}>
            <p class="arm-label">{arm.label}</p>
            <div class="columns">
              {CALLS.map((calls) => (
                <div class="column">
                  <div class="dots" role="img" aria-label={`${arm.counts[calls]} tasks took ${calls}${calls === 7 ? " or more" : ""} tool calls`}>
                    {Array.from({ length: arm.counts[calls] }, (_, index) => (
                      <span style={`--d: ${index}`} />
                    ))}
                  </div>
                  <span class="calls">{calls === 7 ? "7+" : calls}</span>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
      <figcaption>
        Tool calls per task over {piBenchmark.trials} matched tasks each. One dot is one task.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <dl class="figures" data-stagger>
      <div data-reveal>
        <dt>tasks passed, both versions</dt>
        <dd>{piBenchmark.optimised.passed}/{piBenchmark.trials}</dd>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        <dt>fewer tool calls</dt>
        <dd><span data-count>{fewer}</span>%</dd>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        <dt>slower at the median, so far</dt>
        <dd>{slower} s</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <p class="body" data-reveal>
      Pi is an open-source coding agent. I built a separate DeepSeek profile for it that pins the
      model and stops the agent re-checking code that already passes its tests. Both versions solved
      every task; mine got there in fewer steps. The median task is still slightly slower, and that
      is what I'm working on now.
    </p>
  </article>

  <article class="item" aria-labelledby="jev-title">
    <header>
      <h3 id="jev-title">A quicker browser agent</h3>
      <p class="status">Jev Ultrafast, on TypeSafe's Jev decision model. Going public soon.</p>
    </header>

    <figure class="race" data-reveal>
      {
        lanes.map((lane) => (
          <div class="lane" style={`--run: ${lane.seconds * REPLAY}s; --share: ${lane.seconds / jevChecks.serialSeconds}`}>
            <span class="lane-label">{lane.label}</span>
            <span class="track"><span class="bar" /></span>
            <span class="time">{lane.seconds.toFixed(1)} s</span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
      <figcaption>
        {jevChecks.checks} browser checks, replayed at a fifth of real speed.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p class="body" data-reveal>
      My version adds a second engine. It checks in code whether each step actually worked, falls
      back to a safer option when Jev isn't confident, and caches decisions it has already made.
      Checks can run side by side, each in its own browser tab. The browser tests for this site
      run on it.
    </p>
    <p class="body" data-reveal>
      I also keep <a href="https://github.com/AkshayReddyGujjula/jev-knowledge">jev-knowledge</a>,
      a reference any coding agent can load to build with Jev without redoing the research.
    </p>
  </article>
</div>

<style>
  .work {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  .item {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 1.75rem;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line);
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .status {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .body {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  /* Waffle histograms: each column stacks one dot per task, filling bottom-up. */
  .waffles {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .arm {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 6.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: end;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .arm-label {
    padding-bottom: 1.6rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .column {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    justify-items: center;
  }

  .dots {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap-reverse;
    align-content: flex-start;
    gap: 3px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 4.6rem;
    min-height: 1px;
  }

  .dots span {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .optimised .dots span {
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .calls {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  :global(.js) [data-reveal] .dots span {
    opacity: 0;
    scale: 0.4;
    transition:
      opacity 300ms var(--ease-out),
      scale 300ms var(--ease-out);
    transition-delay: calc(200ms + var(--d) * 14ms);
  }

  :global(.js) [data-reveal][data-shown] .dots span {
    opacity: 1;
    scale: 1;
  }

  .figures {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--line);
  }

  .figures div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column-reverse;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }

  dd {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  dt {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  /* The race: bars fill for the measured time, scaled, like a timing screen. */
  .race {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .lane {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8.5rem minmax(0, 1fr) 3.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .lane-label {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .track {
    height: 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .bar {
    display: block;
    width: calc(var(--share) * 100%);
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--ink);
    transform-origin: left;
  }

  .lane:last-of-type .bar {
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .time {
    text-align: right;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  :global(.js) [data-reveal] .bar {
    scale: 0 1;
    transition: scale var(--run) linear 400ms;
  }

  :global(.js) [data-reveal][data-shown] .bar {
    scale: 1 1;
  }

  @media (max-width: 64rem) {
    .work {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .arm {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .arm-label {
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }

    .figures {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .lane {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 3.5rem;
    }

    .lane .track {
      grid-row: 2;
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
</style>
